/**
 * Hardcoded Firebase configurations for each environment.
 *
 * These configs are used by:
 * 1. Vite plugin (Node.js) - to exchange refresh tokens for ID tokens
 * 2. Browser SDK - to initialize Firebase for Firestore access
 *
 * SECURITY NOTE: Firebase web API keys are designed to be public. They are NOT
 * secret keys. Security is enforced via:
 * - Firebase Security Rules (control read/write access)
 * - Authentication (users must sign in)
 * - HTTP referrer restrictions (configure in Firebase Console)
 *
 * These same keys are already shipped in the CLI binary (cli/venus_cli/Constants.cs).
 * Google's documentation explicitly states that Firebase API keys are safe to
 * expose in client-side code.
 *
 * TODO: Consider reading Firebase config from ~/.venus/config.json instead of
 * hardcoding here. This would require updating the CLI (cli/venus_cli) to write the config
 * for the selected environment. Benefits: SDK wouldn't ship with keys, config
 * would come from the authenticated CLI.
 */

